{
	"_about": "The regulars' houses, on the restaurant's side of the street either side of it (see Town and House). Each stands 'at' [x, z] with its front door toward the street (+z, the camera's side); street scenery (trees, bushes) in the way is hidden. A house unlocks ('unlock', a flag in GameState.unlocks) when its regular invites the chefs over (a closing scene in scenes.json, once they first reach Stage 2); before that it's there but locked, with no name on it. After hours the chefs can knock once a restaurant day per house. Visits grow with the regular's stage: porch_stage and up, a chat on the porch; inside_stage and up, they ask everyone in (chefs within porch_radius of the door come along; the room is built far away at 'inside_at', like the beach); items_stage and up, their personal things inside can be looked at ('items'). Below porch_stage the door stays shut with a polite line (house_not_tonight); at dark_stage and lower (or once they're gone) the lights are off and nobody answers. Gifts come in a takeout bag, packed at the restaurant's takeout counter: a cooked dish, or one thing from the pantry (caught or gathered). Giving one floats up how much friendship it added (points), or that the day's cap is reached (capped). A favourite adds favourite_points friendship, something they like liked_points, anything else other_points; gifts add at most daily_cap a day per regular, and each chef can give gifts_per_visit per visit. 'favourites' and 'likes' list dish, fish or forage ids, or 'kind:<kind>' (e.g. kind:fish). 'text' is what the chefs see that isn't a regular's line ({name} is the regular's name, {names} the same with 's or ' on the end, {item} a thing's). Models are '<dir>/<name>' with dir from model_dirs. Outside, decor and patches are [x, z] (or [x, y] on the front wall) from the middle of the house; inside, [x, z] from the middle of the room (the door is at +z, toward the camera), with 'height' off the floor; 'size' is a model's width, 'turn' degrees.",
